  "decision_summary": "Predicted low: the query is atorvastatin, whose absolute oral bioavailability is below 20% in humans. The only low-F statin evidence (pravastatin, F=18%) supports this, while high-F analogues (fluvastatin, cerivastatin) are less transferable due to structural and metabolic differences.",
